# Root environment file — DOCKER COMPOSE + DEPLOY SCRIPTS ONLY.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE
#   * the variables docker-compose.yml interpolates (below), and
#   * the inputs scripts/research-deploy.sh requires from the environment.
#
# WHAT DOES NOT BELONG HERE
#   Everything the api-server reads. That list lives in
#   artifacts/api-server/.env.example — the single documented source of truth
#   for DATABASE_URL, SESSION_SECRET, PORT, APP_*, ALLOWED_ORIGINS,
#   SECURE_CORS, SESSION_COOKIE_*, JSON_BODY_LIMIT, OTP_LENGTH, LOG_LEVEL,
#   S3_* (other than the two MinIO root keys below), PUBLIC_OBJECT_SEARCH_PATHS,
#   PRIVATE_OBJECT_DIR, SMTP_*, MAIL_*, GOOGLE_*/APPLE_* OAuth, GROQ_API_KEY,
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY, CF_ACCOUNT_ID, CF_EMAIL_TOKEN, APP_PUBLIC_URL,
#   TOUR_MEDIA_DIR, MAX_IMAGE_SIZE_MB.
#   Those vars used to be duplicated in both files, which guaranteed drift.
#   Do not re-add them here; add them to the package that reads them.
#
# CLOUDFLARE WORKER (research/)
#   Its bindings (API_BACKEND_URL, GROQ_API_KEY, …) are documented in
#   research/.env.example.

# ---- Docker Compose: Postgres -------------------------------------------------
# Consumed by docker-compose.yml. Dev-only defaults: change both before running
# anything that is reachable from a network.
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
POSTGRES_DB=mednexus

# ---- Docker Compose: MinIO root credentials -----------------------------------
# Consumed by docker-compose.yml (MINIO_ROOT_USER / MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD). This
# bucket holds PHI: radiology images, patient documents, database dumps and
# backups. `minioadmin` is MinIO's published default — fine only because
# docker-compose.yml binds MinIO to 127.0.0.1. Generate a real key for anything
# else:  openssl rand -hex 24
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin

# ---- scripts/research-deploy.sh (production deploy) ---------------------------
# This script has NO dev fallbacks and refuses to start without these:
#   S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID / S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY  must not be minioadmin:minioadmin
#   DATABASE_URL                             must not point at localhost while
#                                            NODE_ENV=production
# Export them in the shell (or `set -a; . ./.env; set +a` after filling this
# file in). Meanings and defaults: artifacts/api-server/.env.example.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@db-host:5432/mednexus
# SESSION_SECRET=<32+ random bytes>
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=<admin password; a random one is generated and printed if unset>

# ---- Object storage prefixes (shared by dev + deploy) -------------------------
# LEGACY read-path lookups: the api-server resolves objects uploaded under the
# historical /mednexus/... and /objects/... layouts. New writes go only to
# <bucket>/radiology/<object-id>. See STORAGE.md for the canonical scheme.
# scripts/dev.sh reads these from this file (it no longer hardcodes its own
# values, which used to contradict this file and research-deploy.sh).
# Canonical list + per-value notes: artifacts/api-server/.env.example.
PUBLIC_OBJECT_SEARCH_PATHS=/mednexus
PRIVATE_OBJECT_DIR=/mednexus

# ---- OAuth sign-in -----------------------------------------------------------
# Social sign-in for the /auth page (Google + Apple). Fill these from your own
# GCP / Apple developer consoles; the provider redirects back to
# https://research-center.fit/api/auth/oauth/<provider>/callback.
# Canonical definitions: artifacts/api-server/.env.example.
#
# A previous revision of this file committed a LIVE Google client ID and client
# secret. A committed client secret must be treated as compromised and rotated:
# anyone with repo history could mint tokens for it. Never put a real value here.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://research-center.fit/api/auth/oauth/google/callback

APPLE_CLIENT_ID=
APPLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
APPLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://research-center.fit/api/auth/oauth/apple/callback